 109: ### D-E — Fixture and contract: mirror Auth's verification state, judge nothing
 110: `_fixture.ts`: `AuthUser` gains `emailConfirmedAt: string | null` and
 111: `verificationLink: string | null`. An email/password registration starts unconfirmed and mints
 112: a link value (the fixture's stand-in for the emailed link the mail catcher would hold). A
 113: provider registration (Google/GitHub) starts confirmed — the expected GoTrue behaviour when the
 114: provider vouches for the address. **This mirror is UNBOUND by this item** (gate-1 ruling [1],
 115: section 7): no OAuth app or credential exists in this environment, so no live provider session
 116: is obtainable — the same recorded gap that leaves the OAuth handshake itself unproved at every
 117: tier, stated in the fixture header since the predecessor. No test this item reads a provider
 118: user's verified state; both new bodies register by email/password. If the prediction is wrong —
 119: a real provider user arriving unconfirmed — the shipped gate fails closed: it refuses, never
 120: allows. The fixture header's mirror section states all of this; the mirror is bound by the
