===== .taskmaster/docs/acceptance/at-req-001.md =====
   1: # AT-REQ-001 — User Authentication & Org Membership
   2: 
   3: Source: prd-mvp.md REQ-001 (+ Promise §9 acknowledgment cadence; NFR Security/audit). Dependencies: none.
   4: 
   5: **Boundary note [cx]:** REQ-001 owns *identity capture* on acknowledgments. The acknowledgment **content gates** (first-funding/match-acceptance copy and non-reuse, Promise §9) are tested in AT-REQ-006; the volunteer first-match-consent disclaimer in AT-REQ-007; time-bounded file links + current-membership checks in AT-REQ-032.
   6: 
   7: ## A. Signup & sign-in
   8: 
   9: - **AT-001.01 (P0)** — Given a visitor, When they sign up as an NGO via email/password, Then an account with global type `NGO` is created, an org membership with the `admin` role is created for their NGO, and the ToS + Platform Promise acknowledgment is required and recorded (timestamp, IP, text version) before any project creation is possible; a later sign-in with the same email/password succeeds. [cx]
  10: - **AT-001.02 (P0)** — Given a visitor, When they sign up via GitHub OAuth as a volunteer, Then an account with global type `volunteer` is created, the GitHub identity is linked to it, and a later sign-in via GitHub returns to the same account. [cx]
  11: - **AT-001.03 (P0)** — Given a visitor, When they sign up via Google as either account type, Then the account is created and sign-in via Google succeeds on return visits.
  12: - **AT-001.04 (P0)** — Given a visitor completing volunteer signup by email or Google (no GitHub identity yet), When they attempt to finish signup without linking a GitHub account, Then completion is blocked with the GitHub-link requirement stated; linking completes signup.
  13: - **AT-001.05 (P0)** — Given a volunteer signup where GitHub is linked, When the link completes, Then volunteer GitHub onboarding fires [cross: REQ-007]: the linked handle AND the imported public stats (top languages, repository count, contribution summary) are observably populated on the profile — a queued-but-empty import fails this test. [cx]
  14: - **AT-001.06 (P0)** — Given an existing account of type `volunteer`, When it attempts an NGO-only action (create an org profile / project need), Then the action is rejected — one account holds exactly one global type; the NGO path requires a separate account.
  15: - **AT-001.07 (P0)** — Given a provisioned `platform admin` account, When it signs in, Then it authenticates and carries the `platform admin` global type; the public signup surfaces offer only NGO/volunteer. [cx r2: verify the type exists + authenticates, rather than only asserting an unstated no-signup rule]
  16: - **AT-001.08 [retired — cx: the PRD defines no identity-collision/linking policy; re-add if the PRD ever specifies one]**
  17: 
  18: ## B. Email verification
  19: 
  20: - **AT-001.09 (P0)** — Given a fresh email/password signup of EITHER account type that can register by email (NGO and volunteer), When the account is created, Then it is email-unverified until the emailed verification link is used; using it flips the account to verified. [cx r2: parameterized over account types]
  21: - **AT-001.10 (P0)** — Given an unverified NGO account, When it attempts to send any Discovery message, Then the attempt is blocked with verification named as the remedy [cross: REQ-002/004].
  22: - **AT-001.11 [retired — cx r2: verification-link expiry/single-use/resend semantics are not stated in REQ-001]**
  23: - **AT-001.38 (P0)** — Given a registered email/password account, When sign-in is attempted with the correct email but an incorrect password, Then it is rejected and no authenticated session is created. [cx r2: wrong-password negative path]
  24: 
  25: ## C. Sessions & password reset
  26: 
  27: - **AT-001.12 (P0)** — Given a signed-in user, When their session expires or is revoked, Then access ends: the next request requires re-authentication (no stale-session writes) [NFR Security].
  28: - **AT-001.13 (P0)** — Given an active session, When the user works continuously, Then the session refreshes automatically without forced re-login mid-work.
  29: - **AT-001.14 (P0)** — Given a user who requests a password reset, When they complete the emailed reset flow, Then the new password works and the old one does not. [cx: audit claim dropped — password resets are not in the PRD's audit list]
  30: - **AT-001.15 [retired — cx r2: reset-link expiry/single-use semantics are not stated in REQ-001]**
  31: 
  32: ## D. Two-layer authorization & multi-NGO
  33: 
  34: - **AT-001.16 (P0)** — Given an NGO-type user, When they belong to two different NGOs, Then membership and role are held per-NGO, and acting in NGO A never grants access to NGO B's data.
  35: - **AT-001.36 (P0)** — Given an account that is `admin` in NGO A and `member` in NGO B, When it performs an admin-only NGO-side action, Then it succeeds in A but is rejected in B — "NGO admin" means the admin role *in that NGO*. [cx r2: exercises the `member` role + role-dependent authz]
  36: - **AT-001.37 (P0)** — Given a volunteer account, When any path attempts to grant it a per-NGO role, Then it is rejected — per-NGO roles are NGO accounts only. [cx r2: NGO-accounts-only restriction]
  37: - **AT-001.17 (P0)** — Given v1 single-seat NGO, When the NGO account attempts to invite or add a second member to its org, Then no such capability exists (UI absent; API rejects).
  38: - **AT-001.18 (P0)** — Given the single NGO account with each action's own preconditions met (vetted for funding, valid lifecycle state, an active match where required [cross: REQ-002/005.5]), When it performs each NGO-side action (funding, acknowledgment, scope edit, volunteer offboarding), Then all succeed under the one account — no action requires a second seat. [cx]
  39: - **AT-001.19 (P0)** — Given any acknowledgment moment, When the acknowledgment is submitted, Then the record captures the acting person's name, title, and authority attestation. [cx r2: non-reuse conjunct removed — owned by AT-REQ-006]
  40: - **AT-001.39 (P0)** — Given an acknowledgment submitted with any one of name / title / authority attestation omitted, When submitted, Then it is rejected and no acknowledgment record is created. [cx r2: the "every acknowledgment captures" guard, negative path]
  41: - **AT-001.20 (P0)** — Given acknowledgment copy, When displayed, Then shared credentials are stated as prohibited and an org email is recommended. [cx: promoted P1→P0 — explicit REQ clause]
  42: 
  43: ## E. Tenant isolation & visibility
  44: 
  45: > **Resolved [founder, d65]:** the platform admin's role spans all accounts (operations/support), so NGO data is visible to its own account, the assigned volunteer, AND the platform admin. REQ-001 wording updated.
